# A trailing slash matches DIRECTORIES only. install.sh creates `node_modules`
# as a symlink into the harness deployment, so this package's dsh imports
# resolve on the same module instance the running host loaded — so the bare name
# is required here, or the link would be committed.
node_modules
node_modules/

*.log

# The private, machine-specific companion to the public MAINTENANCE.md.
# It holds proxy ports, UNC paths and account names — nothing that may be
# published. The public handover doc points to it by name only.
MAINTENANCE-NOTES.md

# Scratch notes for someone mid-task on this machine. Not documentation, and
# not for publication; a live peer conversation pointed out that they were
# one `git add -A` away from being committed.
*.scratch.md
VERIFY-*.md

# Incoming defect reports. They quote REAL conversation titles and session ids
# from whichever conversations filed them, so they must never be committed —
# `MAINTENANCE.md` carries the sanitized findings and the fix. Confirmed the
# hard way: one was swept in by `git add -A` and had to be removed before the
# tag was pushed.
*问题报告*.md

# Incoming debug drops: a defect report plus the Host files extracted from the
# desktop app's app.asar as evidence. The report quotes real session ids, titles
# and Windows paths, and the evidence files are third-party source — neither may
# be published. Findings land in MAINTENANCE.md instead.
debug/

# The marker list for scripts/privacy-scan.sh. It names this machine's users,
# paths and session titles — the very things the scan exists to keep out — so it
# can never be committed itself.
PRIVACY-PATTERNS.txt

# Incoming review/audit documents, same rule. The lasting record is the VERIFIED
# result in MAINTENANCE.md: this class of document is a set of claims, and the
# 2026-09-30 one contains two that did not survive verification — the duplicate
# install row was said to be a hard load failure (§十一之四) and `package.json.meta`
# was recommended for display text, which the Host never reads (§十一之七).
*建议*.md
.DS_Store
PRIVACY-ACCEPTED.txt
